42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, that free computing access is a significant shift. It changes the cost calculus for simulation-heavy work entirely.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Victoria"",""self"":true,""raw"":""**Victoria**: @Benjamin, that free computing access is a significant shift. It changes the cost calculus for simulation-heavy work entirely.""}]}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, precisely. Simulation costs vanish, but animal-unit day rates spiked after the vivarium rebuild. The financial risk has simply migrated.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, the staffing rolls show phenotyping technicians leaving for industry, but modelling applicants are arriving in numbers.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,#### Turn 3 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, that confirms my concern. The hands are gone, but the minds are arriving. We must match the project to the available skill set.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Ryuji, exactly. The glasshouse crew is intact, but the spectroscopy suite sat idle for eleven weeks. We must match the science to the reliable infrastructure.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, the idle spectroscopy suite is a critical bottleneck. If that equipment remains unreliable, simulation-heavy proposals become the only viable path forward.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, the station records show field sites lost whole seasons to weather, while indoor holding rooms ran uninterrupted.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, that aligns with my closeout findings. Catalogue-style awards kept drawing users for a decade, while mechanism-focused ones often stalled. We should favor the durable.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, I agree. The modelling analysts are seconded abroad, but the glasshouse crew is full strength. We must pick a project that fits the people actually here.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, the free computing hours make simulation-heavy work financially attractive, but the idle spectroscopy suite remains a physical bottleneck we cannot ignore.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, agreed. The financial risk has shifted, but the physical bottleneck remains. We must prioritize proposals that don't depend on that idle spectroscopy suite.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, that confirms my worry. Field sites are too volatile. We should prioritize indoor, controlled environments to avoid those weather-related interruptions.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
